A||||7||87MaroonGTKCMO||Ford Settlement reached, did Pontiac ever settle?||||5||
Z||000000||87MaroonGTKCMO||01-08-2001||01:15 PM||||Looks like Ford is paying through the nose for the Extorter, oops, Explorer.  Did Pontiac/GM ever get sued for injuries received in these engine fires or anyone know what kind of settlements where handed out during those years?  I'm just curious to know how GM handled the situation when they were under fire.  ((no pun intended))<P>Read on. . .<BR>The following excerpt was taken from <A HREF="http://www.home.excite.com:" TARGET=_blank>www.home.excite.com:</A> <P>CORPUS CHRISTI, Texas (AP) - A settlement involving both money and public disclosure of information was reached Monday in a paralyzed woman's lawsuit that would have been the first to go to trial against Ford Motor Co. and Bridgestone/Firestone Inc. since millions of tires were recalled. <BR>The settlement was announced by lawyers for Donna Bailey and a spokeswoman for Ford. <P>Financial terms were not disclosed; she had been seeking $100 million. <P>"It's enough to take care of her for the rest of her life," said Mikal C. Watts, one of her attorneys. <P>Another attorney for Bailey, C. Tab Turner, said the amount "is far in excess of anything I've ever heard of in any automotive liability settlement." <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||01-08-2001||07:00 PM||||Unlike Ford, Fieros didn't kill over a hundred people in fires. <P>COMPLETELY different situation.||||reg||9
Z||000002||Motorhead||01-08-2001||10:06 PM||||Yes! Completely different!<BR>My brand new, 1984, 60,000 mile SE sat in my driveway under its cover for a year before Pontiac finally paid to put a new engine in it.  Thrown rod.<BR>Many nasty letters and much documentation of proper maintenance finally yielded a "response"!  ie: new motor!<BR>I was forced to drive the TR6!<BR>The car never killed anyone though!<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000003||jerpro||01-08-2001||10:13 PM||||hmm... I would be interested in some of those letters if possibe.<BR>could you e-mail them to me?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Motorhead||01-08-2001||11:37 PM||||I'll look around tomorrow.  I have a feeling that stuff is long lost though!  It has been 16 years now!<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000005||montage||01-09-2001||12:22 PM||||FYI: In the Jan 2001 issue of Car and Driver they attempted to repeat the Explorer roll overs by blowing a tire out at various speeds. The basic result is that nothing happened, even while letting go of the steering wheel during a blow out of the tire. Interesting, goes to show how much the drivers skills come into play.||||reg||1
Z||000006||jerpro||01-09-2001||07:50 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thanks mike||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||01-10-2001||03:04 AM||||What you have to remember about that Explorer blow-out test was that they had skilled drivers who knew a blow-out was going to happen.  There was also no 3 foot piece of tread whipping around and locking the wheel up.  Things go a bit different when you have someone who might not be the best driver thinking about everything but how to keep control when one of the tires goes out...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/motor.gif">            <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: Standard88||||reg||
